    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 23.087583333333335,
      "end": 36.718625,
      "lesson_progress": 0.2727272727272727,
      "text": "Success criteria. I can explain what the percent symbol means. I can represent a familiar percentage using a hundred-part model. I can compare percentages by thinking about the same whole.",
      "chapter": "Success Criteria: I can…",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [
        "1. Explain what the percent symbol means.",
        "2. Represent a familiar percentage using a hundred-part model.",
        "3. Compare percentages by thinking about the same whole."
      ],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "success_criteria"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 36.718625,
      "end": 50.85279166666667,
      "lesson_progress": 0.36363636363636365,
      "text": "Percent means per hundred. One hundred percent is one complete whole. Fifty percent is half of that whole. Always identify the whole: a percentage describes a share of it, rather than a count by itself.",
      "chapter": "Build the idea",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "explanation"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 50.85279166666667,
      "end": 61.525958333333335,
      "lesson_progress": 0.45454545454545453,
      "text": "A battery at seventy-five percent represents seventy-five of one hundred equal parts of full capacity. It is more than half full but less than completely full.",
      "chapter": "Example 1: plan",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [
        "75% = 75 out of 100",
        "50% < 75% < 100%"
      ],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "explanation"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 61.525958333333335,
      "end": 71.90108333333333,
      "lesson_progress": 0.5454545454545454,
      "text": "The percentage bar shows the same relative share: three quarters of its complete length. The full bar always stands for the same full battery in this comparison.",
      "chapter": "Example 1: explain",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [
        "75% = three quarters of the whole"
      ],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "explanation"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 71.90108333333333,
      "end": 81.542875,
      "lesson_progress": 0.6363636363636364,
      "text": "Compare forty percent and sixty percent of the same whole. Imagine forty shaded cells and sixty shaded cells on equal hundred-grids.",
      "chapter": "Example 2: plan",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [
        "40% = 40 out of 100",
        "60% = 60 out of 100"
      ],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "explanation"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 81.542875,
      "end": 90.992125,
      "lesson_progress": 0.7272727272727273,
      "text": "Sixty percent is the greater share because sixty of the same-sized parts is more than forty. Both shares use a common scale of one hundred.",
      "chapter": "Example 2: explain",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [
        "60% > 40%"
      ],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "explanation"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 90.992125,
      "end": 99.39833333333333,
      "lesson_progress": 0.8181818181818182,
      "text": "Which is closer to a complete whole: ninety percent or twenty-five percent?",
      "chapter": "Your turn",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [
        "90% ? 25%"
      ],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "question",
      "pause": 4
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 99.39833333333333,
      "end": 110.04675,
      "lesson_progress": 0.9090909090909091,
      "text": "Ninety percent is only ten of the hundred parts below the whole. Twenty-five percent is seventy-five parts below it. Ninety percent is closer.",
      "chapter": "Let’s check",
      "equation": [],
      "board": [
        "100% − 90% = 10%",
        "100% − 25% = 75%"
      ],
      "rows": [],
      "line": null,
      "area": null,
      "context": null,
      "note": "",
      "role": "answer"
    },
    {
